# The state-dir allow-list: G0 `state_files` (the lint check_no_state_files, see
# docs/development/ipc-shared-memory.md) and gate rule STATE-1.
#
# Every game<->sidecar and Lua<->Lua contract lives in shared memory; the native module spawns
# and stops our processes by handle and reads tool output through pipes; dev control is the
# DevCtl ring (hsmp-tools ipc-ctl). So a state dir holds ONLY:
#   [config ...]    persistent config
#   [identity ...]  the player / server identity
#   [log ...]       logs and dev output (diagnostic dumps)
# plus [runtime: <config|identity|log>] globs written at run time (STATE-1 only, never Lua
# literals), [fs: ...] server/src modules allowed to write files (std::fs / tokio::fs), and
# [debt: <owner>] contracts not yet moved to shared memory (delete the names once moved). Any
# other category fails G0 `state_files`, as does a Lua literal naming an unlisted file.
# A bare name is a state-dir file name (or name prefix / `{}` / `<id>` pattern) that
# mods/**/*.lua may name in a string literal; STATE-1 also accepts it in a run's listing.
# The list only ever SHRINKS: `hsmp-gate state-files --update` drops unused entries.

[log] the event log (hsmp_log.lua) and its rotation marker
.rotating

[config] persistent config, not IPC (design D9)
.settings.json
.my_character.json
.gi_backup.txt
.browser_prefs.txt

[log: dev output] diagnostic dumps and probe logs (HSMP_DEV / gate only; written, never read back)
.tdiag_recv.txt
.tdiag_send.txt
.probe_recv
.probe_send.txt
.diag_
.state_dump_
.willie_dump_
.world_scan.txt
.parity_results.txt

[runtime: log] logs written at run time by the game, the sidecar and the harness (STATE-1 only)
hsmp_events*.jsonl
hsmp_events*.jsonl.rotating
.career_guard.jsonl
.sidecar_panic.log
sidecar*.jsonl

[identity] the player key file (the listen host passes it to its server as --owner-key-file)
.player_key

[runtime: identity] the player identity and pinned server keys (STATE-1 only)
identity
known_servers.json
# a listen host's server inherits HSMP_STATE_DIR and keeps its identity there
server_identity.key

[fs: logs] event logs, the panic log, and the --report zip written next to the logs
fs:server/src/events.rs
fs:server/src/sidecar/panic_guard.rs
fs:server/src/server_report.rs

[fs: career guard] career-save backups and the guard log (+ the state dir itself at start)
fs:server/src/sidecar/career_guard.rs
fs:server/src/sidecar/main.rs

[fs: identity] the player / server identity keys and pinned server keys
fs:server/src/net/mod.rs
fs:server/src/sidecar/net.rs

[fs: tap] the dev/gate IPC tap (a log, not IPC)
fs:server/src/sidecar/ipc_shm.rs

[fs: hsmp-server] the dedicated server's / master's own files (ban list, admin, the hosting --pid-file; not a game state dir)
fs:server/src/proc_util.rs
fs:server/src/server/admin.rs
fs:server/src/server/tick.rs
